Subject: [PATCH] CompleteDismount guards falling flags and bounds ground search

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

In mod-playerbots CompleteDismount (src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp),
two defects were observed:

1. Under a live MoveFall descent spline, CompleteDismount stripped
   MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING | MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING_FAR unconditionally two lines
   after MoveFall() set it. For a bot sharing its Player with a connected
   client (such as a streamed realm), the server tells the client it is not
   falling during the descent whose landing packet Player::HandleFall will be
   billed for. When MoveFall() declined, clearing the flags is necessary so
   stale flight/falling flags do not block MMAP routing. The cleanup must only
   run when MoveFall() did not commit to a descent. MoveFall returns void, so
   whether it committed must be inferred: sampling spline ID before and after,
   along with isFalling() and !Finalized(), correctly identifies a committed
   descent even when the bot was already falling before the dismount.

2. MoveFall() internally invokes GetMapHeight with MAX_FALL_DISTANCE
   (250000.0f), which is unbounded. On vmap geometry (bridges, docks, buildings)
   where height search resolves to terrain underneath the surface the bot
   stands on, that unbounded search commits to an uncapped descent that kills
   the character in a single hit. Probing with DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH (50.0f)
   bounds the settling search to a distance a dismount can legitimately settle
   over, preventing MoveFall from inventing an unasked-for fatal drop.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream mod-playerbots bounding the MoveFall dismount settle distance and
guarding the MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING cleanup so it only clears flags when MoveFall
declined to commit to a descent.

APPLIES TO

quadseven/mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130,
on top of local patches 0001-0018. Touches only CompleteDismount in
src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp
index 4157e0f..40320aa 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/CheckMountStateAction.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include "DBCStores.h"
 #include "Event.h"
 #include "GameTime.h"
+#include "MoveSpline.h"
 #include "PlayerbotAI.h"
 #include "PlayerbotAIConfig.h"
 #include "PlayerbotSpellRepository.h"
@@ -281,30 +282,27 @@ void CheckMountStateAction::CompleteDismount(Player* bot)
 
     float const startZ = bot->GetPositionZ();
 
-    // Settle the bot on the ground when it was dismounted in mid-air. MoveFall()
-    // is the whole job on its own: it returns when no valid height is found, and
-    // aborts when the ground is already less than 0.1 yards away, so a bot that
-    // dismounts standing on solid footing is left untouched.
+    // Settle the bot on the ground when it was dismounted in mid-air.
     //
-    // MAX_FALL_DISTANCE IS NOT A SAFETY BOUND, and the comment that used to sit
-    // here said it was. It is 250000.0f, commented "unlimited fall" at
-    // GridTerrainData.h:28. So where the 50 yard default would have refused to
-    // find a surface, this finds one arbitrarily far down and MoveFall commits
-    // to the whole descent. On vmap geometry - a dock, a pier, a bridge, a
-    // building floor - where the height search resolves to the terrain
-    // UNDERNEATH the surface the bot is standing on, that descent is a drop the
-    // world never asked for.
-    //
-    // That matters more than it looks, because it is the half of the old bug
-    // that was left standing. The removed HandleFall() block probed with
-    // UpdateAllowedPositionZ, whose search is DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH (50 yards),
-    // so it was capped at 0.018 * 50 - 0.2426 = 65.7% of maximum health per
-    // dismount and needed two inside the regeneration window to kill. This call
-    // has no such cap. The fix stopped fabricating the damage and left the code
-    // that can fabricate the fall, and a bot that shares its Player with a real
-    // connected client will have that manufactured drop billed back to it for
-    // real, as a MSG_MOVE_FALL_LAND the client sends on landing.
-    bot->GetMotionMaster()->MoveFall();
+    // BOUND THE GROUND SEARCH TO A LEGITIMATE DISMOUNT SETTLING DISTANCE
+    // (DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH, 50.0f yards). MoveFall() internally searches with
+    // MAX_FALL_DISTANCE (250000.0f), which is unbounded: on vmap geometry
+    // (bridges, docks, buildings) where the height search resolves to terrain
+    // underneath the surface the bot stands on, or high in the air, that
+    // unbounded search commits to an uncapped descent that kills the character
+    // in a single hit. Probing with a legitimate settling bound prevents
+    // MoveFall from inventing an unasked-for fatal drop.
+    float const groundZ = bot->GetMapHeight(bot->GetPositionX(), bot->GetPositionY(), startZ, true, DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH);
+    bool committed = false;
+    if (groundZ > INVALID_HEIGHT && (startZ - groundZ) <= DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH)
+    {
+        uint32 const splineIdBefore = bot->movespline ? bot->movespline->GetId() : 0;
+        bot->GetMotionMaster()->MoveFall();
+        committed = bot->movespline &&
+                    (bot->movespline->GetId() != splineIdBefore) &&
+                    bot->movespline->isFalling() &&
+                    !bot->movespline->Finalized();
+    }
 
     // Rebase the fall baseline on the spot the bot dismounted at, so a fall is
     // never measured from a stale, much higher Z. MoveFall() does this itself
@@ -348,15 +346,16 @@ void CheckMountStateAction::CompleteDismount(Player* bot)
     // so nothing is lost by letting the next packet re-base it.
     bot->SetFallInformation(GameTime::GetGameTime().count(), startZ);
 
-    // OPEN QUESTION, DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED HERE. When MoveFall() has just
-    // committed, this clears MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING two lines after MoveFall() set
-    // it, while its spline is still running - so the server tells a connected
-    // client it is not falling during exactly the descent whose landing packet
-    // gets billed. Making it conditional needs a reliable "did MoveFall commit"
-    // signal, MoveFall() returns void, and getting that guard wrong reintroduces
-    // the stuck flight flags this function exists to clear. It is filed rather
-    // than guessed at.
-    bot->RemoveUnitMovementFlag(MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING | MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING_FAR);
+    // Only clear MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING and MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING_FAR when MoveFall()
+    // declined to commit to a descent. When MoveFall() has committed, the spline
     // is running, and stripping the falling flags desyncs connected clients and
+    // confuses landing accounting. When it declined, clearing them cleans up
+    // stale flight/falling flags so MMAP routing is unblocked.
+    // Checking the spline ID generation, isFalling(), and !Finalized() correctly
+    // determines whether MoveFall() launched a new descent spline even if the
+    // bot was already falling before the dismount.
+    if (!committed)
+        bot->RemoveUnitMovementFlag(MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING | MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING_FAR);
 
     // DO NOT call Player::HandleFall() here, and do not reintroduce a
     // UpdateAllowedPositionZ()-derived "ground" to feed it. That is what this
